# Story page: labyrinth
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Heart of the Maze
---
At the center of everything lies a maze with no edges, no exits and no manners, and every wall in it seems to remember {name}, like a teacher who has been disappointed before.

At its heart is a vast coil of shimmering scales, with no head, no tail and no end. I had hoped for something smaller. One always does.

And {name} understood at last that the shimmers had never been lights. They were memories, and the memories were its own.
